From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-ssdk: fix sfp.h union visibility and remaining missing prototypes

sfp.c includes sfp.h before sfp_reg.h, but sfp_reg.h is what defines
union sfp_*_u.  GCC reports every prototype in sfp.h as using a union
"declared inside parameter list", and with -Werror that is fatal:

  include/hsl/sfp/sfp.h:42:23: error: 'union sfp_dev_type_u' declared
    inside parameter list will not be visible outside of this definition
  src/hsl/sfp/sfp.c:103:1: error: conflicting types for 'sfp_encoding_get'

Include sfp_reg.h first; adpt/sfp/adpt_sfp.c already does.

Two more files define functions with no prototype:
 - adpt_hppe_stp.c: adpt_hppe_stp_init() is declared in adpt_hppe.h but
   the file never includes it.  port_state_get/set() are local to the
   file and have no header entry, so make them static.
 - ref_port_ctrl.c: six helpers are only used in this translation unit;
   make them static.  qca_ar8327_sw_mac_polling_task() is called from
   ssdk_interrupt.c, which carries its own extern, so declare it locally.

src/adpt/hppe/adpt_hppe_stp.c:27:1: error: no previous prototype for
  'adpt_hppe_stp_port_state_get' [-Werror=missing-prototypes]
src/ref/ref_port_ctrl.c:239:5: error: no previous prototype for
  'qca_ar8327_vlan_recovery' [-Werror=missing-prototypes]
src/ref/ref_port_ctrl.c:570:6: error: no previous prototype for
  'qca_ar8327_sw_mac_polling_task' [-Werror=missing-prototypes]

